1 id: patient identification number
3 age: age in years
4 sex: sex (Male; Female)
5 dataset: dataset from UCI Heart Disease database (Cleveland; Hungary; Switzerland; VA Long Beach)
6 cp: chest pain type
-- Value 1: typical angina
-- Value 2: atypical angina
-- Value 3: non-anginal pain
-- Value 4: asymptomatic
7 trestbps: resting blood pressure (in mm Hg on admission to the 
hospital)
8 chol: serum cholestoral in mg/dl
9 fbs: (fasting blood sugar > 120 mg/dl)  (True; False)
10 restecg: resting electrocardiographic results
-- Value 0: normal
-- Value 1: st-t abnormality (having ST-T wave abnormality (T wave inversions and/or ST 
            elevation or depression of > 0.05 mV))
-- Value 2: lv hypertrophy - (showing probable or definite left ventricular hypertrophy
            by Estes' criteria)
11 thalach: maximum heart rate achieved
12 exang: exercise induced angina (1 = yes; 0 = no)
13 oldpeak = ST depression induced by exercise relative to rest
14 slope: the slope of the peak exercise ST segment
-- Value 1: upsloping
-- Value 2: flat
-- Value 3: downsloping
15 ca: number of major vessels (0-3) colored by flourosopy
16 thal: (normal; fixed defect; reversable defect)